    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580-a1">

                <pb facs="0578" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg480"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thackara to Mr.
                            Hill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havre France</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    of the death by accidental drowning of Howard Linwood Ridlon, a landsman
                    belonging to the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Hartford</hi>, on September 27
                    last.</p>
                <p>The deceased was buried with military honors in the Sainte Marie Cemetery of
                    Havre on September 29, 1900.</p>
                <p>The French Government officials most promptly acceded to my request for
                    permission to land an armed firing party from the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hartford</hi>, and sent a delegation of soldiers to the funeral,
                    representing the infantry, artillery, and maritime gendarme services.</p>
                <p>In answer to my letter of thanks I have received a most courteous reply from the
                    commandant d’armes, the highest military officer in command at Havre.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Thackara</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">U. S. Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
